  "notes": "Often confused with {貯金|ちょきん}. While {貯金|ちょきん} specifically refers to money deposited in a bank, {貯蓄|ちょちく} is broader and includes all forms of accumulated financial assets such as stocks, insurance, and property. {貯蓄|ちょちく} is more commonly used in formal, economic, and financial planning contexts. Common collocations: {貯蓄|ちょちく}を{増|ふ}やす (increase savings), {貯蓄|ちょちく}を{取|と}り{崩|くず}す (dip into savings), {貯蓄率|ちょちくりつ} (savings rate).",
